{"parentUuid":"aec44b58-cfea-445f-97cb-5fc9ece72140","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6d5c0a1d-fdd5-4db0-8cbd-a5c82a0adcb7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014fkMEFXBGKL11hwZb6fTam","type":"tool_result","content":"/* Meteora — bloom.\n\n   The scene renders into a half-float buffer (three's output buffer), so\n   engine flames, bolts, fireballs and the sun keep their real brightness\n   until the final tone mapping. This pass lets the brightest of it bleed\n   into its surroundings the way it does in a lens: the image is cut above\n   a soft threshold and shrunk through a chain of ever smaller targets with\n   a wide filter, then grown back up with a tent filter, each level adding\n   to the next (the bloom of Jimenez's \"Next Generation Post Processing in\n   Call of Duty: Advanced Warfare\"). The result is added to the scene before\n   three tone-maps it.\n\n   The first shrink averages each 2 × 2 block weighted by 1 / (1 + luma),\n   so a single white-hot pixel (a bolt's core, a star) does not flicker into\n   a blob as it crosses pixel boundaries. */\n\nimport * as THREE from 'three';\n\n\nconst VERTEX = /* glsl */ `\nvarying vec2 vUv;\nvoid main() {\n  vUv = uv;\n  gl_Position = vec4(position.xy, 0.0, 1.0);\n}`;\n\nconst DOWN = /* glsl */ `\nuniform sampler2D tSrc;\nuniform vec2 uTexel;\nuniform bool uFirst;\nuniform vec3 uCurve;      // threshold − knee, 2 × knee, 0.25 / knee\nuniform float uThreshold;\nvarying vec2 vUv;\n\nfloat luma(vec3 c) { return dot(c, vec3(0.2126, 0.7152, 0.0722)); }\nvec3 s(vec2 o) { return texture2D(tSrc, vUv + uTexel * o).rgb; }\n// A block's colour, weighted down by its brightness (Karis).\nvec4 karis(vec3 c) { float w = 1.0 / (1.0 + luma(c)); return vec4(c * w, w); }\n\nvoid main() {\n  vec3 a = s(vec2(-2.0, 2.0)), b = s(vec2(0.0, 2.0)), c = s(vec2(2.0, 2.0));\n  vec3 d = s(vec2(-2.0, 0.0)), e = s(vec2(0.0)), f = s(vec2(2.0, 0.0));\n  vec3 g = s(vec2(-2.0, -2.0)), h = s(vec2(0.0, -2.0)), i = s(vec2(2.0, -2.0));\n  vec3 j = s(vec2(-1.0, 1.0)), k = s(vec2(1.0, 1.0)), l = s(vec2(-1.0, -1.0)), m = s(vec2(1.0, -1.0));\n  vec3 col;\n  if (uFirst) {\n    vec4 sum = karis((j + k + l + m) * 0.25) * 0.5\n      + karis((a + b + d + e) * 0.25) * 0.125 + karis((b + c + e + f) * 0.25) * 0.125\n      + karis((d + e + g + h) * 0.25) * 0.125 + karis((e + f + h + i) * 0.25) * 0.125;\n    col = sum.rgb / max(sum.a, 1e-4);\n    // The soft threshold: a smooth knee instead of a hard cut.\n    float br = max(col.r, max(col.g, col.b));\n    float rq = clamp(br - uCurve.x, 0.0, uCurve.y);\n    rq = uCurve.z * rq * rq;\n    col *= max(rq, br - uThreshold) / max(br, 1e-4);\n  } else {\n    col = e * 0.125 + (a + c + g + i) * 0.03125 + (b + d + f + h) * 0.0625 + (j + k + l + m) * 0.125;\n  }\n  gl_FragColor = vec4(max(col, 0.0), 1.0);\n}`;\n7:   a soft threshold and shrunk through a chain of ever smaller targets with\n95:// Five levels reach about a tenth of the screen; a sixth, a few pixels\n97:export function createBloom({ strength = 0.25, threshold = 1, knee = 0.7, spread = 1, levels = 5 } = {}) {\n98:  const LEVELS = levels;\n173:/* Whether this browser can render into half-float targets (and so keep the","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"351f1df1-73d6-4e4e-92bd-3773d8439f59","timestamp":"2026-10-21T15:54:49.983Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"/* Meteora — bloom.\n\n   The scene renders into a half-float buffer (three's output buffer), so\n   engine flames, bolts, fireballs and the sun keep their real brightness\n   until the final tone mapping. This pass lets the brightest of it bleed\n   into its surroundings the way it does in a lens: the image is cut above\n   a soft threshold and shrunk through a chain of ever smaller targets with\n   a wide filter, then grown back up with a tent filter, each level adding\n   to the next (the bloom of Jimenez's \"Next Generation Post Processing in\n   Call of Duty: Advanced Warfare\"). The result is added to the scene before\n   three tone-maps it.\n\n   The first shrink averages each 2 × 2 block weighted by 1 / (1 + luma),\n   so a single white-hot pixel (a bolt's core, a star) does not flicker into\n   a blob as it crosses pixel boundaries. */\n\nimport * as THREE from 'three';\n\n\nconst VERTEX = /* glsl */ `\nvarying vec2 vUv;\nvoid main() {\n  vUv = uv;\n  gl_Position = vec4(position.xy, 0.0, 1.0);\n}`;\n\nconst DOWN = /* glsl */ `\nuniform sampler2D tSrc;\nuniform vec2 uTexel;\nuniform bool uFirst;\nuniform vec3 uCurve;      // threshold − knee, 2 × knee, 0.25 / knee\nuniform float uThreshold;\nvarying vec2 vUv;\n\nfloat luma(vec3 c) { return dot(c, vec3(0.2126, 0.7152, 0.0722)); }\nvec3 s(vec2 o) { return texture2D(tSrc, vUv + uTexel * o).rgb; }\n// A block's colour, weighted down by its brightness (Karis).\nvec4 karis(vec3 c) { float w = 1.0 / (1.0 + luma(c)); return vec4(c * w, w); }\n\nvoid main() {\n  vec3 a = s(vec2(-2.0, 2.0)), b = s(vec2(0.0, 2.0)), c = s(vec2(2.0, 2.0));\n  vec3 d = s(vec2(-2.0, 0.0)), e = s(vec2(0.0)), f = s(vec2(2.0, 0.0));\n  vec3 g = s(vec2(-2.0, -2.0)), h = s(vec2(0.0, -2.0)), i = s(vec2(2.0, -2.0));\n  vec3 j = s(vec2(-1.0, 1.0)), k = s(vec2(1.0, 1.0)), l = s(vec2(-1.0, -1.0)), m = s(vec2(1.0, -1.0));\n  vec3 col;\n  if (uFirst) {\n    vec4 sum = karis((j + k + l + m) * 0.25) * 0.5\n      + karis((a + b + d + e) * 0.25) * 0.125 + karis((b + c + e + f) * 0.25) * 0.125\n      + karis((d + e + g + h) * 0.25) * 0.125 + karis((e + f + h + i) * 0.25) * 0.125;\n    col = sum.rgb / max(sum.a, 1e-4);\n    // The soft threshold: a smooth knee instead of a hard cut.\n    float br = max(col.r, max(col.g, col.b));\n    float rq = clamp(br - uCurve.x, 0.0, uCurve.y);\n    rq = uCurve.z * rq * rq;\n    col *= max(rq, br - uThreshold) / max(br, 1e-4);\n  } else {\n    col = e * 0.125 + (a + c + g + i) * 0.03125 + (b + d + f + h) * 0.0625 + (j + k + l + m) * 0.125;\n  }\n  gl_FragColor = vec4(max(col, 0.0), 1.0);\n}`;\n7:   a soft threshold and shrunk through a chain of ever smaller targets with\n95:// Five levels reach about a tenth of the screen; a sixth, a few pixels\n97:export function createBloom({ strength = 0.25, threshold = 1, knee = 0.7, spread = 1, levels = 5 } = {}) {\n98:  const LEVELS = levels;\n173:/* Whether this browser can render into half-float targets (and so keep the","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"0ba57a7a-f494-40e1-9f6c-fc2b560478e4","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass/fun/hedgerow","root":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass","branch":"hedgerow-grass","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"voho/protocodus.github.io","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"voho/protocodus.github.io","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"voho/protocodus.github.io","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass/fun/hedgerow","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"aec44b58-cfea-445f-97cb-5fc9ece72140","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass/fun/hedgerow","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"hedgerow-poc","slug":"shimmying-swimming-falcon"}
