kyLight with the flare's light).\n- 0fd7339d smoke plumes ~90 m over each fire (plumes.js, new; main.js creates G.plumes, draws it\n  in the late pass like flames.js, updates it per frame with the wind, lightning and the flare).\n\nTried and shelved: eye adaptation in the grade pass (a 1x1 half-float ping-pong stalls: the\nper-frame step is under half-float resolution; and the flare-lit meadow measures inside the\nnormal night range, so it would not have tamed that glare). WIP copy in the session scratchpad.\n"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"5593022e-c58e-4190-b2ac-8dcfad95caf6","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgFfR415EDafJE8aoR83m","requestRef":"e01cd77d-9e13-412e-aa90-c1f514d617e9","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"15becc98-2823-4cd3-8d97-1c994c4da6c1","timestamp":"2026-10-21T16:02:05.755Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"hedgerow-poc","slug":"shimmying-swimming-falcon"}
