{"parentUuid":"5c19b120-8856-4eb6-aad0-d56bd7ea43a0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgFgJrrYwRxEhxFVK9dHS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I made five more graphics commits on `hedgerow-grass`, each a separate improvement, plus the searchlights round from before. Each was checked in a headless browser on the real GPU, and the node checks pass after each one. Each merges cleanly into `hedgerow-poc`, and nothing is pushed.\n\n- **e356d66b, rooms behind the lit windows** (new `rooms.js`): the lit windows were flat glowing panels that blew out to white. When the game loads, it finds each window pane in the houses' textures and draws a room behind it: papered walls, beams overhead, a table under a lamp that casts real shadows, a cupboard, and lace half-curtains in some windows. The room shifts with your viewpoint as you walk past. It costs about 0.3 ms when a café front fills the screen.\n- **c995938e, cloud deck**: the overcast now has rolling shapes, and the clouds over the burning farms glow orange from below. The sky is also now only drawn where it actually shows, which makes it cheaper in most views.\n- **e8872629, rain**: the near streaks are pixel-thin instead of fat white strokes. Faint rain now also falls in the distance, out to about 60 m, so it shows down the street in the lamp and fire light. A burning flare lights all of it up.\n- **0fd7339d, smoke plumes** (new `plumes.js`): each fire now sends a column of smoke about 90 m up, leaning downwind and lit orange at the base. Before, the smoke stopped at a dozen metres.\n- **e2ce56a0, explosions** (new `fireball.js`): a grenade used to turn the whole screen white for a fifth of a second, then almost disappear. Now it shows a turbulent fireball that cools into a grey-brown smoke cloud. To get there I lowered the blast light in `combat.js`, made muzzle flashes and blast lights fade faster, and capped how bright nearby lights can make smoke and dust.\n\n**Things to know:**\n- The smoke cap applies to all lit smoke, so smoke beside street lamps is somewhat dimmer than before. The truck fire's smoke still looked right when I checked.\n- I tried automatic eye adaptation (exposure that adjusts to bright and dark scenes) and dropped it. It got stuck because of a number-precision limit, and it wouldn't have fixed the main problem anyway: the meadow turns snow-white under a flare. That glare is still there.\n- As before, the anti-aliasing commit 2c09b946 must be merged together with its fix a0b204b2.\n\nThe shared notes list every commit. The test server, headless browser and my `launch.json` entry are all removed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":345,"cache_read_input_tokens":572100,"output_tokens":877,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":345,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":877,"cache_read_input_tokens":572100,"cache_creation_input_tokens":345,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":345},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"9b7cbbbc-fb3b-4b44-b495-cc5b4e6fc497","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgFgJrKZL1batTDCs3px6","requestRef":"74370ac6-1360-4b3b-828a-f7c6919cb113","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"wrap_up","type":"assistant","uuid":"236f8400-615d-4358-8129-82b6a0b098d1","timestamp":"2026-10-21T16:13:49.951Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus